docs/fidelity.md:89:- Auto Cannon5003 and Seeker Flak5004 fire at their retained target, then acquire the next target. Their first eligible call acquires without firing; equal-distance acquisition chooses the last candidate. Auto aiming uses the nearest mounted detail and rounded flight prediction. Flak's source seeker scan does not filter by enemy ownership. Orbital slots do not reset their cooldown when already full. Firing sound uses the owning field's5→0→-1 counter and only friendly projectile insertion; pause freezes that counter while wall-timed rockets can still be created. Browser-clock firing throttling was removed, matching the earlier collection/hurt separation.
docs/fidelity.md:99:- `AvatarInterface.Run` performs input/shooting and HUD motion before `_‑dI`, then `BTAGameWorld.Run` calls the field and avatar in that order. Ordinary full-health upgrades and higher-level deaths are checked on the next interface frame, after shots/pickups from the previous field update. A higher-level lethal hit can therefore be healed by a pickup before the downgrade check. `_‑Zx.Damage` handles level-zero death separately and starts `_‑1E(true)` synchronously, resetting life to1. `_‑Ud` resolves center/diagonal ties in left→right→top→bottom order with strict comparisons; center escapes left, not down. The recreation keeps a single active crossing when repeated lethal impacts arrive during the escape.
